From ab5dae20743fe4d53c037ee826675e0c3d10c349 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Agnya <manthram@Pradass-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:14:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Send a welcome email on new account creation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds sendWelcomeEmail() to server/auth/email.ts, reusing the existing
nodemailer/SMTP transporter and EMAIL_FROM pattern already used for
verification codes and magic links (server/auth/email.ts). Requires
SMTP_HOST/SMTP_USER/SMTP_PASS to be set (e.g. Resend's SMTP relay) and
a verified hibowan.com sending domain — falls back to a console log
in development when those aren't set, matching sendVerificationCode's
existing dev-mode behavior.

Wired into both OAuth "create new user" branches in
server/auth/passport.ts — confirmed via App.tsx that these are the
only live signup paths on the site today (Clerk's sign-in components
are commented out as "temporarily disabled", and the custom
email/magic-link path in server/auth/email.ts has no reachable UI).
Facebook signups usually come back with no email, so the send is
skipped rather than attempted. Fire-and-forget with a caught/logged
error in both call sites: a failed send must never block or fail the
login the user is actively waiting on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 server/auth/email.ts    | 88 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 server/auth/passport.ts | 17 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 104 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/server/auth/email.ts b/server/auth/email.ts
